WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:03.440
Wait, please!

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.530
I understand how you feel,

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.110
but guerrilla recruitment isn't allowed!

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.320
Huh? It's not?

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.320
<b>Passionately Welcoming
Earth Sciences Club 
New Members</b>

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:14.800
Sorry.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.190
We got a little ahead of ourselves.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.660
For now, let's get you both
 back to the classroom.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.620
<b>Class 2-5</b>

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.640
I'll get permission from the school.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.360
Once we have that, we can all 
recruit as much as we want.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.440
Okay!

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.730
I'll have to decorate this 
sign more in the meantime.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:33.630
More?

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.000
Hey, hey!

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.840
Oh, Suzu-chan.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:37.800
Huh?!

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.340
Making a spectacle of yourselves 
so early in the new school year, eh?

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.040
It was the talk of my class, too, 
so I got too embarrassed and came here.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.040
Suzu-san, your hair!

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.290
What happened to it?

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:53.110
Oh, you haven't seen it, 
have you, Ino-senpai?

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.530
As of this spring, I've been reborn.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.570
I'm Suzu Version 2!

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:02.290
It does look good on you, 
but it's awfully sudden.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.000
She was growing it out all this time 
because she admired my sister.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.740
Yeah.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.160
But when I talked to Misa-nee,

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:15.030
she told me to treasure myself 
instead of admiring her.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:19.890
As a result, business is booming at Suzuya 
thanks to Suzu-chan's upgraded look.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.620
Jeez, I owe so much to Misa-nee.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.850
You tend to make a spectacle 
of yourself, too, Suzu-san.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:30.060
So what was that parade about earlier?

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.810
Starting this year, there are only three 
of us in the earth sciences club,

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.030
so I want to make sure our club 
will continue after we graduate.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.510
Wow, you're actually sounding 
like a vice president.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:42.490
Yeah.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.730
Also, we'll be able to get more 
funding if we have more members.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:47.870
Wow.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.800
I-It's not like that!

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.880
We weren't hoping to buy an equatorial 
mount with the new members!

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.340
Oh?

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.340
All right, then, today we'll work out 
a plan for recruiting members.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.220
Okay.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.310
I-I'll do my best!

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.270
Excuse me.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.730
<b>Club Member
 Recruitment Plan</b>

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.730
Oh, come on in.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.450
I'd like to join the earth sciences club.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.190
Same here.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.370
Huh?

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:50.500
10. Rain With Occasional Fortune-Telling

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.410
We haven't formally started recruiting yet, 
and we already have people wanting to join?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.750
I wonder if our parade 
this morning worked.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.960
I'm a first-year, Nanami Yuu.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.100
Same, Sakurai Chikage.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.950
Sakurai?

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.640
S-Sakura-senpai's younger sister?!

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.590
Thank you for taking care
 of my older sister last year.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.560
Now that I see you, you look just like her!

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.040
Nice to meet you, Ino-senpai.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.450
S-Same!

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:20.640
Oh, I heard you participated 
in the Earth Science Olympiad!

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.280
I participated, too...

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.880
Yes, you were loud.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:29.510
Mira-senpai, Ao-senpai. 
I hope we'll have a good year together, too.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.290
Huh?

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.500
You know about us?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.260
Yes.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.580
You're both with the astronomy group, right?

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.090
You know a lot about our earth sciences club.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:43.090
My sister often talked 
about all of you at home.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.550
She said she had a lot of fun, 
and you were good club members.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.140
Uh, so I assume you're hoping to join 
the geology group, Chikage-chan?

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:54.520
Yes. I fell in love with rocks 
thanks to my sister.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:57.940
I also like power stones 
and fortune-telling.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.940
<b>Geomancy
 Fortune-Telling</b>

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.060
That's reassuring!

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:04.400
I'm sure it'll be a big hit in our newsletter
 and at the cultural festival!

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.200
You're just as cute as 
my sister said you were.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:13.650
Oh, uh, we should explain for you, Nanami-san.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:17.520
We have two groups in our club: 
the geology group and the astronomy group.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.570
I know.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.880
I came to see you at the 
cultural festival last year.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.530
You were here?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.760
Did you have fun?

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:24.980
Yes.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:27.760
But, frankly, I thought it was a bit lacking.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.280
Yoo-hoo!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.070
Megu said she wanted to look 
in on the earth sciences club,

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.660
so I brought her here...

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.980
Looks like things are awkward.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:41.360
Oh. This is Suzu-san, a second-year,

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.920
and her younger sister, Megu-san.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:44.300
They're not club members,

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.950
but they helped us make the sweets 
for the cultural festival.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.890
Your sweets were the best!

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:52.160
Aw, what a sweet, honest girl.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:56.620
Um, so about what you were saying... 
What was lacking?

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.750
Your displays for the cultural 
festival were all well-made,

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.580
and your sweets were both 
delicious and wonderful.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.090
But...

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:08.190
As the earth sciences club, 
I think you should be more aware of issues.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:10.790
Aware of issues?

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.980
What I want to pursue isn't geology 
or astronomy, but meteorology.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:20.090
I want to approach our club activities 
with a sense of duty toward learning

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.770
more about weather and climate,
 in order to help others.

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.660
To help others, huh?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.660
Nanami-san seems like 
a very responsible girl.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.370
That's a new field and a new goal.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.910
I wonder if our current earth sciences club

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:43.340
can help Nanami-san realize 
what she hopes to achieve.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.310
Don't hold back. Eat up.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:53.740
There's plenty more.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.260
Thank you so much.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:56.490
Here!

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:57.730
Thanks.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.890
I'm starting to learn what you like, Ao!

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.330
Oh, that's right. You both got letters.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:06.250
From the National Astronomical Observatory.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.280
I hope we can discover an asteroid!

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:16.490
<b>Shining Star 
Challenge</b>

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.780
The problem is the required short essay.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.490
Only seven people get 
to participate, after all.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.890
We've been studying hard every 
day and gathering information,

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.560
so I'm sure we'll be fine.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.460
Yeah.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.380
My feelings about space and the stars, huh?

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:34.650
<i>When I first met Ao, 
I wanted to learn more about the stars.</i>

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.300
<i>Once I joined the earth sciences club,</i>

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:41.520
<i>I learned about rocks and learned how fun 
it can be to share the stars with everyone.</i>

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.730
That's it!

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:46.650
A barbecue?

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:47.680
Yeah!

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.500
I want our two first-years to have
 lots of fun experiences!

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:55.280
So I was thinking we should have a barbecue 
with everyone like we did last year.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.050
That might be a good idea.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.790
Let's talk to Ino-senpai 
and Endou-sensei about it.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:00.790
Yeah!

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.710
I already put it in your schedule.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.420
Of course...

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.150
<b>Class 1-2</b>

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:11.330
<i>This weekend, we're having a barbecue 
to welcome our new members.</i>

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:13.500
<i>Let us know if there's 
anything you'd like to eat.</i>

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.090
Sounds fun.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.280
<i>We'll collect rocks by the riverside</i>

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.090
<i>and observe the stars and moon 
while eating delicious food!</i>

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.080
<i>They're all so carefree.</i>

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.770
I want to toast marshmallows

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:26.570
Uh...

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.850
She's actually surprisingly cute, huh?

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.760
<b>Sparkle</b>

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.660
White marshmallows, yellow 
marshmallows, pink marshmallows!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.960
That sounds like a tongue twister.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.820
Mira, I think you bought 
too many marshmallows.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.830
I want to make Nanami-san happy!

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.080
Star Marshmallows

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:47.080
<i>I guess she got that bag for herself.</i>

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:49.990
That just leaves preparing the food.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:50.730
Yeah!

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:54.050
It's been so long since we had 
a barbecue. I can't wait!

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:01.090
The weather report said 
it would just be cloudy!

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:03.130
Maybe we should postpone it.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.310
But we already bought so much food...

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:07.090
<i>Location change!</i>

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:08.760
<i>I'll meet you all at the station!</i>

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.230
<i>I called Suzu, too!</i>

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:11.080
Sensei...

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.150
That's our barbecue magistrate!

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.280
<i>See you later!</i>

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:19.700
I see.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:22.250
We won't have to worry about the rain here.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.580
The weather was already like this 
when I woke up this morning.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:26.700
I didn't want to reschedule, either,

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.590
so I quickly searched for places 
we could hold it in the rain.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.480
Thank you again this year, Suzu-san.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:34.550
No, no, don't worry about it.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.120
Anyway, I'll leave the rest in your hands.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.300
Wake me when the meat's done.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.550
Huh?

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:46.120
I can't believe it's raining on our 
first event of the new school year.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.520
It's fine.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:50.520
I brought lots of tissues with me!

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:53.160
Oh! I get it!

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.650
You're so cute, Ino-senpai!

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.730
I'm sure it'll clear up if we make a bunch!

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.150
Let's make them together!

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:04.420
I think we should start getting 
the barbecue set up instead...

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.960
They're just as easygoing as my sister said.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:24.100
You all seem used to this.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.610
We did this last year and the year before.

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:29.770
Actually, this exchange 
feels sort of nostalgic...

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:34.270
If we'd hosted it at the riverside, we could 
have collected rocks and stargazed...

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:36.670
But we can't do either here.

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:38.610
I'm sorry, Nana-chan, Chika-chan.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:40.700
Chika-chan?

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:41.620
Nana-chan?

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:45.580
The way she just gives everyone 
a nickname is nostalgic, too.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:48.540
Something smells good.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.210
What are you making?

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:54.750
You'll see.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:03.100
The meat's so good.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:04.660
Isn't it?

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.830
It's totally different 
when you eat it outside.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:08.060
Though...

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:12.020
Looks like it's really pouring down now.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.890
I think it'll stop in an hour or two, though.

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:18.540
Nana-chan, can you predict the weather?

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:18.990
Huh?

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:22.260
I'm good at predicting it with my shoe!

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.190
No, um...

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.800
I just looked at the forecast 
on my smartphone.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.670
You'll get your shoe dirty.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:31.790
Oh, right.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:35.460
That was so good!

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.080
Nanami-san, you want to focus on meteorology,

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.970
which includes weather reporting, right?

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.090
Of course.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:45.410
It includes everything related to weather.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:49.350
The wind, clouds, atmosphere, 
even natural disasters.

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:52.310
Uh, you make it sound like
you don't like it much.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:56.060
Of course not. Not after my 
relatives suffered because of it.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:56.820
Huh?

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.820
The truth is, three years ago...

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.920
My relatives' home suffered flood damage.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.410
Fortunately, no one was injured,

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.240
but I never want to see my 
aunt make that face again.

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:11.710
That must have been terrible.

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:15.670
That's why I need to be 
able help other people.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.510
Nanami-san...

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.470
You can have this.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.470
It's blue lace agate,

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.230
also known as sky blue onyx.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:33.130
It helps calm emotions and relax the spirit.

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:36.810
You shouldn't push yourself too hard.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.520
I'm not really pushing myself.

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.480
What's that? Some kind of charm?

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.820
You have a wrinkle on your forehead.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.620
Thanks, I suppose.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:53.000
Meteorology is a field that's 
really close to home for you, huh?

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:56.150
Well, it's more helpful 
than geology or astronomy,

00:12:56.150 --> 00:13:00.250
since it's used to predict the 
weather and prevent disasters.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.960
Astronomy helps people, too,

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.040
by launching artificial satellites 
that improve our lives

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:08.010
and watching small astronomical bodies 
and debris to see if they'll hit Earth.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.970
Geology can help in daily life, too.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.030
Uh...

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:15.000
No examples are coming to mind right now!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:19.850
It helps with predicting earthquakes and 
excavating oil and mineral resources.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:23.440
Some stones have the power 
to make people happy, too.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.220
That last one isn't exactly geology.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:27.410
No.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.370
All of our photos, videos, 
and letters were ruined by the mud.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:38.660
Aunt...

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:41.960
<i>I hate the rain.</i>

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:47.340
<i>I hate that filthy, foul-smelling mud, 
and I hate how useless I am.</i>

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:50.690
<i>I'm just doing what I have to do.</i>

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.060
The rain finally let up, huh?

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.840
Making so many was worth it!

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:59.540
Hey, that's...

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.230
Look, Nana-chan! There's a rainbow!

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.940
Oh, a circumhorizontal arc!

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:07.400
Circumhorizontal?

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:12.120
In atmospheric optics, that's called 
a circumhorizontal arc, not a rainbow.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:16.840
The light is refracting off of hexagonal 
ice crystals to create the rainbow colors.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:18.830
It's a fairly rare phenomenon.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:22.590
This is actually my first 
time seeing the real thing.

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:31.760
Wow, I see!

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.760
Hey, I know! Let's take a picture!

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:34.320
Yeah!

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.520
I want to put this in our newsletter!

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:39.140
You've studied an awful lot, Nanami.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:39.500
Mira-chan, Ao-san, please line up over there!

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:40.470
Okay!

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.140
Here I go!

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:43.940
I have a goal. It's only natural.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:45.220
Yay!

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:45.400
Yeah,

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.680
but I think studying for the 
sake of others is incredible.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:53.470
I just wish you would cherish
 your own feelings a little more,

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:57.370
especially the part 
of you that finds it fun.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:00.360
Your wrinkle's gone.

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:04.880
If we don't take the picture quickly, 
it'll disappear, Nanami-san.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:08.780
They already gave me the nickname, 
so Nana's fine.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.420
Let's go, then, Nana-chan.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.230
Everyone!

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.450
The baumkuchen's ready!

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:17.770
Baumkuchen?!

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:21.970
Incredible!

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:22.940
It's perfect!

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:25.820
Let's eat!

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.260
This has great strata!

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:31.700
It's bent here, so it's a folded strata!

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:35.450
"Baum" means "tree," so aren't these age rings?

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.410
Nana-chan, that's rude.

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:42.240
I'm glad you're enjoying it!

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:45.680
By the way, what are these 
creepy-colored marshmallows?

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:48.710
Huh? I didn't buy any 
marshmallows that color.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.360
Nana-chan, you burned them.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:01.330
That was fun.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:04.480
I need to prep for tomorrow, 
so I'll be taking off now.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.690
Okay, thanks for today.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:11.690
I just wish this weather had come sooner.

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:12.500
All right.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:15.540
Why don't we try sticking 
it out a bit longer?

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:21.480
On days when the weather is nice,
 we practice using a telescope like this.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.470
Go ahead.

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:26.450
The moon is pretty.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:27.170
Right?

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:29.700
The one you see next to it is Jupiter.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:32.630
What magnification are we seeing it at?

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:34.450
Oh, uh,

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.420
the lens barrel's focal 
length is 910 millimeters,

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:41.780
and the ocular lens is 
15 millimeters thick, so, uh...

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:44.390
With this lens, the magnification 
is about 60x power.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.810
I know. Let's adjust the angle.

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:49.770
Got it!

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:53.370
You can take pictures like 
this on your smartphone, too?

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.600
It's called a collimated photo.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:59.340
It's hard if you're not familiar with it, 
but you're good at it, Nanami-san.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.510
Nana's fine.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:07.220
Speaking of which, you two,
how are your short essays coming along?

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:08.420
Short essays?

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:14.880
<b>Shining Star 
Challenge</b>

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:11.270
The Shining Star Challenge?

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:14.880
The short essays are essentially 
the test to qualify for participation.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.940
They're not done yet,

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:19.610
but we're polishing them up 
together every night.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:20.850
Every night?

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.880
Are you delinquents, 
walking around late at night?

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:29.580
Ao-senpai is currently living away 
from her parents with Mira-senpai

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:33.640
so they can discover an 
asteroid together, right?

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.200
I heard it from my sister.

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:37.830
Away from her family...

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:41.490
It's not easy to take a 
bold step like that, is it?

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.540
What? What's the matter?!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.740
Onee-chan...

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:50.900
What's that?

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:52.650
Earth fortune-telling.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:54.670
It's called geomancy.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:58.250
I just wanted to try reading their fortunes.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.630
This is...

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:02.940
Isolation...

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:06.230
But they should take action
 and move forward.

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:11.650
Huh? No way. For real?

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:13.630
<b>From: The National Astronomical Observatory
To: Konohata Mira

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.630
I-I did it!

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:14.600
Ao!

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:16.720
I passed the written screening!

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:17.840
That's incredible!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.550
Wow, congratulations!

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:21.700
That's truly worth celebrating!

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:26.790
I'm going to write an article about it
 as a scoop for the newspaper!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:29.790
We'd love to accompany you there, as well,

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.500
but it's not in our club budget.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.360
So, instead...

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:37.000
I compiled information about the 
special products of Ishigaki Island!

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:39.970
<b>Buy these at 
Ishigaki Island!!</b>

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:39.970
Use it as a reference when buying souvenirs!

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:44.960
Jeez, Senpai, you're getting too 
excited and out of control.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.340
Sorry.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:50.290
I didn't make it.

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.150
Huh?

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.800
U-Um...

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.240
They both look like they've lost their souls.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:01.820
<i>Only one passed? Chika's fortune was spot-on.</i>

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:03.770
I-I'm sorry!

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:06.890
But cheer up! I'm sure there'll 
be another opportunity!

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:09.820
Senpai, you're not being very encouraging!

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:11.090
Senpai...

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.420
<i>Mira! Ao!</i>

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:15.940
<i>What are you two sulking for?</i>

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.050
<i>Yoo-hoo! Long time no see!</i>

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:20.760
Sakura-senpai? Monroe-senpai?

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.690
Senpai, what's wrong?!

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:29.730
It's just way more reassuring 
when our senpai are here.

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:32.440
Chikage told me about it.

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:36.850
You don't have any time to waste 
after clearing that major hurdle!

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:37.630
Yeah.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:40.360
Besides, even if only one of you can go,

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.910
you can still share what you 
learn there with each other, right?

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:46.120
<b>Onee-chan</b>

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:46.120
<i>We're still here to give advice 
if anything happens, too.</i>

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:47.240
Right!

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:49.080
Thank you so much!

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:50.230
Later!

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:54.610
Oh, I forgot to tell Mira congratulations.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:57.410
You haven't changed, Sakura-chan.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:01.160
"While you may feel isolated,

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:04.880
the path before you leads to new stages.

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:08.340
Abandon your old values and go 
forth with faith in your intuition."

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.230
That's your fortune.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:13.790
I hope it's helpful.

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.100
Endou-sensei said she'd be my chaperone.

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:21.480
That's a relief.

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:22.560
I know.

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:28.930
I'd probably get lost if I traveled... 
to Okinawa... all by myself...

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:29.810
Mira?

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:34.170
I wanted us to go together!

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.190
Mira!

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:38.680
You're not acting like yourself.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:42.130
Like everyone already said, 
we have to move forward.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:43.840
R-Right.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.800
I'll try thinking about whether 
 there's anything I can do.

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:51.770
<i>Has Ao gotten stronger?</i>

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:07.190
Well, I'm heading out.

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:08.720
Be careful.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.800
We're looking forward to the results!

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:12.540
Also the souvenirs!

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:22.030
It's going to be lonely for us, too.

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:25.470
It's only for a few days, though.

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:28.490
I'll call you every day!

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.390
It's so hot!

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:37.370
Okay. First, we rent a car...

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:38.200
Mira!

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.740
Ao?!

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:46.650
I... I'm here!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:51.080
<i>Y-You're here? But...</i>

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:53.420
<i>Why?</i>

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.960
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
11. 
Shining Star Challenge!

00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:38.770
Next time, "Shining Star Challenge!"
